Brotli is a generic-purpose lossless compression algorithm developed by Google.
It combines a modern variant of LZ77, Huffman coding, and 2nd-order context
modelling to achieve compression ratios comparable to the best general-purpose
methods available, while remaining fast to decompress.

This KOS port builds the complete library: common (c/common/), decoder
(c/dec/), and encoder (c/enc/).

URL: https://github.com/google/brotli
